{"skill":{"slug":"ordercli","displayName":"Ordercli"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1767545372216,"changelog":"","changelogSource":null,"license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":2087,"sha256":"562f5716faa528b335be627ba00feaa369d0b1a7b41c9bf4e17594864c8b01ef","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1960,"sha256":"2c67cba2b352c5e70db260535ace88ed78bc349898d3b8654d70fb25929c270f","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789013621990,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"d43ca2e2626b26bef1ad3091be28f3b8f8f4109b60d449438985366f620179bd","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/d43ca2e2626b26bef1ad3091be28f3b8f8f4109b60d449438985366f620179bd","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: ordercli\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe skill bundle is suspicious due to instructions in `SKILL.md` that direct the agent to execute commands accessing sensitive browser data. Specifically, `ordercli foodora cookies chrome --profile \"Default\"` and `ordercli foodora session chrome --url https://www.foodora.at/ --profile \"Default\"` instruct the agent to read Chrome browser cookies and session information. While framed as importing for the `ordercli` tool's functionality, this capability represents a significant security risk, as it involves accessing data from another application (Chrome) that could contain credentials or session tokens, making it a potential vector for data exfiltration if the `ordercli` binary itself were compromised or malicious.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159622047},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":28,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789013621990},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill is mostly transparent about using ordercli, but it asks users to install a mutable external CLI and import browser sessions while also enabling cart-changing actions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Food delivery account credentials, authenticated browser sessions, order history, delivery addresses, and cart modification authority are plausible for this CLI, but the browser Default-profile access is under-scoped for the stated purpose.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The install metadata points to a third-party Homebrew tap and a Go module using @latest, so the reviewed artifact does not pin the executable version or integrity for a CLI that handles credentials and sessions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill explicitly documents importing Chrome cookies and session state from the Default browser profile for passwordless Foodora access, which is sensitive and broader than ordinary order lookup.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No system persistence, background service, or tool hijacking is present in the skill file; however, the documented browser profile reuse and session import imply local authentication material may persist in ordercli-controlled storage.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The main description frames the skill as checking past orders and active status, but the artifact also documents reorder commands that add previous orders to a cart with --confirm.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review this skill carefully before installing. Prefer a pinned and verified ordercli version, avoid importing from your main Chrome profile, use a dedicated browser profile if browser login is necessary, and only run reorder commands when you explicitly want cart changes.","findings":"[SDI-1] unexpected: The artifact does disclose the reorder section and says to confirm cart-changing actions, but the top-level purpose remains narrower than the documented cart mutation capability.\n[SDI-1] expected: The description mentions Deliveroo WIP and the commands are marked not working yet, so this is a disclosure issue rather than hidden provider support.\n[YR1] unexpected: Authentication is expected for order lookup, but importing Chrome Default-profile cookies and passwordless sessions is high-impact and insufficiently scoped in the artifact.\n[T08] unexpected: Installing ordercli is expected, but using mutable external install targets without a pinned reviewed version is a material supply-chain concern because the CLI receives credentials and session data.\n[T05] unexpected: Browser-based login may be purpose-aligned, but direct Default Chrome profile cookie/session import exposes sensitive authentication state beyond the minimum needed for checking orders.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789013621990}}}}}